{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788542381550278001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"newborn-ethnologic-scaup","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"593f930344bfdd4bb7a647e373a08584e41ca6babd0ac24b3f7667e724c2427f","event_uuid":"af609d44-9ba1-402d-9a93-52220466a250","position":{"commit_sha":"468e7a26768051f9ed729e99f29ea3e26ad12554","position":"1788524754894611001-af609d44-9ba1-402d-9a93-52220466a250"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c1e4d329355e81afb298bb3ad053104366ac698712cae31d4acaff49f402c29c","event_uuid":"1982e8eb-3449-4fe8-aa33-7944e7e43169","position":{"commit_sha":"3429105e59a03c0a3b8c46b23b152df24f6b3b75","position":"1788524782264705001-1982e8eb-3449-4fe8-aa33-7944e7e43169"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788524754894611001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1982e8eb-3449-4fe8-aa33-7944e7e43169","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"1035-bed7-c855-4732"}],"description":"## Symptom\n\nOn current `origin/main` (69cd2b9e15aa), this passes in the full suite but FAILS when run as\na narrow selection:\n\n    pytest tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py::test_a_marker_in_a_new_gate_scripts_head_admits_it\n    E   ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'scripts._mechanism_delta'\n\nThe failing import is inside `ratchet_head_lines()`:\n`from scripts._mechanism_delta.markers import HEAD_LINES`. It needs the repo root on\nsys.path, which in a narrow selection is not established.\n\n## Bisected\n\n    6b034b9f8224  PASS   (Make scanner-integration recipe POSIX-sh portable)\n    9c7d78127696  FAIL   <- first bad commit: 'Revert scanner-integration Verified gate'\n    cad66dd237cc  FAIL\n    457d9a20bed9  FAIL\n    a220bfafa7ae  FAIL\n    69cd2b9e15aa  FAIL   (current main)\n\nReproduced on a clean detached worktree of unmodified origin/main, so this is not a\nworktree or venv artifact. `import scripts` succeeds at BOTH refs when the repo root is\nexplicitly on sys.path, so the regression is in what puts it there during collection, not in\nthe package itself. The revert deleted scripts/install_review_scanners.py,\n.github/workflows/_scanner-integration.yml and three infra/compose files, and touched the\nMakefile; the mechanism connecting that to collection-time sys.path is the open question.\n\n## Why CI is green anyway\n\nThe default suite runs the whole tree, where something else establishes the import before\nthis module needs it, so `Verified` passes and nothing surfaces. The failure appears only\nwhen a contributor runs the module (or a small set of modules) on its own — which is exactly\nwhat an agent does when told to 'run the three gates make lint does not cover'.\n\nThat makes this a sibling of bug 1035-bed7-c855-4732, in the OPPOSITE direction: 1035 is a\nlocal green on a tree CI rejects; this is a local red on a tree CI accepts. Both erode the\nsame thing — whether a local result can be believed. A test that passes only by grace of\nanother test's import side effect is not a trustworthy oracle either way.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The narrow selection above passes on a clean checkout of main.\n- [ ] The fix makes the import explicit (e.g. the module establishes the repo root on\n      sys.path itself, as scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py already does for its own import)\n      rather than relying on collection order.\n- [ ] A regression test pins that the module passes when run ALONE, so the isolation\n      property is enforced rather than incidental.\n\n## Not claimed by this reporter\n\nFound while rebasing change 2619 (bug 1035). Reported, not fixed: it is unrelated to that\nchange and fixing it there would have bloated an approved change and delayed both.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"7f46-790d-7b9f-4db1","ticket_type":"bug","title":"test_mechanism_delta fails in a narrow pytest selection on main: scripts._mechanism_delta unimportable","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["af609d44-9ba1-402d-9a93-52220466a250","1982e8eb-3449-4fe8-aa33-7944e7e43169"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788542381550278001,"uuid":"37247369-6aae-4011-9388-fdf3876f4d26"}